	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(-337.7777777777778, -528.1045751633985, 1050.0, 70.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="28">A. DATA IMPORT AND EXPLORATORY ANALYSIS</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(59.80048159614722, -350.61919504643964, 486.37426900584796, 160.6432748538012)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="15">Dataset : 569 observations, 30 numerical predictors and a binary diagnosis. ID is retained only as metadata. Distributions, correlations and PCA are inspected before modelling.

No missing data, data set moderetely imbalance (66% benign).
Some features are highly correlated.</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/plain" rect="(-341.11111111111114, 502.2222222222223, 1050.0, 70.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="28">B. SUPERVISED LEARNING</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/plain" rect="(1046.6666666666667, 348.88888888888874, 497.7777777777777, 69.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">INITIAL SCREENING — Ten learners are compared by stratified 10-fold cross-validation on the 70% training partition. Imputation and standardisation are fitted inside each fold.</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/plain" rect="(2235.133020344289, 1463.3020344287952, 449.60876369327116, 115.61032863849823)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">NEURAL-NETWORK TUNING — Architecture and activation are screened first, followed by an alpha regularisation search. The final NN is evaluated once on the untouched 30% test partition.</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/plain" rect="(-268.8888888888888, 2613.3333333333335, 882.7272727272731, 95.90909090909008)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">FEATURE SELECTION — Collinearity filtering (we remove features that are colinear by more than 95% --&gt; 7 features removed) and L1 feature ranking (8 features stand out) are are performed on training data only. The same eight selected variables are then applied to both train and test partitions.</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/plain" rect="(1497.7777777777778, 2806.6666666666665, 1550.0, 105.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">LOGISTIC-REGRESSION TUNING ON 8 FEATURES — A broad L2 C search is followed by a refined search. Hyperparameters are selected from training cross-validation only.</text>
		<text id="7" type="text/plain" rect="(3430.0000000000005, 2363.333333333334, 506.66666666666697, 71.66666666666697)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">FINAL SUPERVISED EVALUATION — Selected LR and NN configurations are tested on the untouched 30% hold-out data. ROC and confusion matrices describe final performance.</text>
		<text id="8" type="text/plain" rect="(-516.6666666666666, 3295.555555555555, 487.7777777777777, 83.33333333333303)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="28">C. UNSUPERVISED LEARNING</text>
		<text id="9" type="text/plain" rect="(-583.3333333333333, 3660.0, 413.3333333333333, 176.66666666666697)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="15">Diagnosis is excluded from clustering inputs and retained only as metadata for post-hoc ARI, NMI and label-alignment evaluation.</text>
		<text id="10" type="text/plain" rect="(400.754716981132, 3499.1194968553455, 519.8113207547169, 70.56603773584948)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">BASELINE CLUSTERING — K-means and Ward are evaluated with internal diagnostics and post-hoc agreement measures.</text>
		<text id="11" type="text/plain" rect="(1293.3333333333335, 3200.0000000000005, 480.0, 76.66666666666652)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">DBSCAN TUNING — Candidate epsilon values are compared while min_samples remains fixed at 5.</text>
		<text id="12" type="text/plain" rect="(71.38364779874178, 5605.9119496855365, 900.0, 90.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">**SPECTRAL TUNING **— We take a number of neighbors of 10 as the baseline then, as we see that the ARI is one of the best, we search for the parameters that increases the ARI and other metrics. 

Finillay the model with n_neighbors = 15 and the assign_label = kmeans, seems the best (ARI = 0.7795) .</text>
		<text id="13" type="text/plain" rect="(2443.3333333333344, 4521.111111111111, 562.2222222222222, 105.5555555555552)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">FINAL CLUSTERING COMPARISON — Silhouette evaluates internal separation; ARI, NMI and best alignment describe post-hoc agreement with diagnosis.</text>
	</annotations>
